(base/'learner-only.md').write_text('''# One switch. Two rooms.\n\nStatus: Draft\n\nYou and Ravi robbed a jewellery store. You’re caught, in separate rooms. Your goal here: fewer prison years. You control your statement. Neither sees the other’s final statement. No contact or enforceable agreement. One fictional decision; switches are labelled what-ifs.\n\nConfess means accepting the invented deal and naming Ravi. Stay silent means refusing the deal. Zero means no prison years. This assigned goal is not a judgment of anyone’s values.\n\n| Your statement | Ravi’s statement | Your years | Ravi’s years |\n|---|---|---:|---:|\n| Silent | Silent | 1 | 1 |\n| Confess | Silent | 0 | 5 |\n| Silent | Confess | 5 | 0 |\n| Confess | Confess | 3 | 3 |\n\nFirst what-if: Ravi stays silent. Choose: **Stay silent** / **Confess**. Your selection is unscored. Then change only your own statement.\n\nSeparate what-if: both confess. If only you become silent while Ravi still confesses, will your years **fall**, **stay**, or **rise**? Unscored.\n\nFrom both confessing, controls available for comparison: **Silence only Ravi** / **Silence both**. These are teaching comparisons, not new control over Ravi in the story.\n\n## Café setting\n\nYou run a café near another owner’s café. Goal: greatest own daily profit—money left after listed costs. Fictional one-day model. Independent choices, neither sees the other’s final choice, no future effects or other costs.\n\n| Your action | Other café | Your profit | Other profit |\n|---|---|---:|---:|\n| Usual prices | Usual prices | ₹5,000 | ₹5,000 |\n| Discount | Usual prices | ₹6,000 | ₹2,000 |\n| Usual prices | Discount | ₹2,000 | ₹6,000 |\n| Discount | Discount | ₹3,000 | ₹3,000 |\n\nStart with both discounting. Other café stays fixed discounting. Choose: **Keep usual prices** / **Run a discount**. Then hold your chosen action while comparing the other café at usual prices.\n\n## Separate cost what-if\n\nEach café running a discount now pays an additional ₹2,000 that day. Usual prices incur none. Everything else stays unchanged. These are final profits after that cost.\n\n| Your action | Other café | Your profit | Other profit |\n|---|---|---:|---:|\n| Usual prices | Usual prices | ₹5,000 | ₹5,000 |\n| Discount | Usual prices | ₹4,000 | ₹2,000 |\n| Usual prices | Discount | ₹2,000 | ₹4,000 |\n| Discount | Discount | ₹1,000 | ₹1,000 |\n\nOther café fixed discounting. Choose: **Keep usual prices** / **Run a discount**. Explain the effect of the added cost while holding the other café fixed.\n''')
